2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/7633706/halver-i-halverson
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Is Held for
2 CONT Halver I. Halverson;
2 CONT Was Born in Norway
2 CONT Funeral services for Halver I. Halverson, who had been living at the home of his daughter, Mrs. L. H. Abbott, 1120 First street southeast, were held Friday afternoon at the Randall funeral parlors. Burial was in Elmwood cemetery. 
2 CONC Mr. Halverson died Monday. Mr. Halverson was born in Stavanger, Norway, in 1858. He came with his parents to Ogle county, Ill. at the age of 12 and later moved to Iowa. In 1887 he was married to Laura Meling, who survivies him. He
2 CONC  and his family lived on a farm near Radcliffe and in 1907 moved to Minnesota, where they lived until a year ago. Then they came to Mason City. He is survived by his widow and nine sons and daughters, Mrs. Frank Kelley, Mrs. L. H.
2 CONC  Abbott, Clarence, Noah, Henry, Lewis and Melvin, all of Mason City; Casper, Hazen, N. Dak.; and Joseph, Elinor, Minn. A brother, Ingavol, Jewel, and 16 grandchildren also survive him. Two brothers, Seivert and Lars, and one siste
2 CONC r, Mary Iverson, preceded him in death.
2 CONT Mason City Gobe-Gazette, Sat., 12/14/1929
