2 CONT Laura J. Erickson, 95, of Minot, North Dakota, formerly of Upham, North Dakota, who died Thursday, May 13 at Trinity Hospital, Minot, North Dakota.   Burial was in Bloomfield Lutheran Cemetery, Upham, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT Laura was born June 17, 1914, on the family farm near Upham, a daughter of Lars and Annie (Lundervold) Lunde. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She attended school in Upham, North Dakota, graduating in 1932. She completed her education at Minot Teachers College, earning her teaching certificate. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Following college, she taught in a rural Granville school for a year. In the late 1930's, she worked in Towner at the Farm Government offices, and then worked two years in the McHenry County Treasurer's office. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Morgan Erickson on June 27, 1943, at Bloomfield Lutheran Church in Upham, North Dakota. The couple made their home in Upham, North Dakota, where they owned and operated Erickson Hardware until 1973. Morgan died April 1
2 CONC 2, 1985. She continued to live in Upham until September of 2007, when she moved to Wellington Assisted Living in Minot, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of Bloomfield Lutheran Church, now New Hope Lutheran Church, in Upham, North Dakota, its WELCA, Ruth Circle, Senior Citizens, and Birthday Club.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by one son, Dwayne, Harker Heights, Texas; two daughters, Jean Thompson, Bismarck, North Dakota,  and Dorothy Peterson, Mohall, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT And 11 grandchildren; two step-grandchildren; nine great-grandchildren; seven step-great-grandchildren; and other relatives.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her parents; husband; five sisters, Gena Lunde, Alma Lunde, Bertina Holm, Adeline Kirkeby, and Alice Smith; one brother, Oliver Lunde; and a son-in-law, Keith Fleck.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * U.S. Social Security Death Index
2 CONT * Laura J Erickson
2 CONT * Birth:	June 17 1914
2 CONT * Death:	May 13 2010
2 CONT * Last residence:	Minot, North Dakota
2 CONT ----
