2 NOTE Just in case the caption is too hard to read, I am suggesting that these two pictures depict the same house; the left one in about 1910 and the right one in 1962 after years of not being maintained. This is to say, that the folks 
3 CONC believed that this was the original homestead site from their childhood when they took the picture in 1962 (8 mm video). The buildings are identical, location of windows and doors are the same, I don't see the cellar entry which c
3 CONC ould be hidden by the horses in the1910 picture. Both of them have a similar size lean-to back entry or storm entry towards the barn. The chimney is in the correct place, though a little shorter than is shown on the 1910 picture. 
3 CONC The 1910 picture also has another outbuilding close by, which has been removed by the time of the1962 picture.
