1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/person-3005906_740933041_740933041/lizzie-maria-thompson MyHeritage Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 20 2021, 19:56:25 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/person-3005906_740933041_740933041/lizzie-maria-thompson MyHeritage Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 20 2021, 20:22:05 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Lizzie Maria Thompson Surdahl
2 CONT BIRTH
2 CONT 16 Apr 1887
2 CONT Belford Township, Aurora County, South Dakota, USA
2 CONT DEATH
2 CONT 23 Jan 1978 (aged 90)
2 CONT Bottineau, Bottineau County, North Dakota, USA
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT Oak Creek Cemetery
2 CONT Bottineau, Bottineau County, North Dakota, USA
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID
2 CONT 198774093 ·
2 CONT
2 CONT Lizzie Thompson was born on a farm in Belford Township near Storla, SD. She moved with her family to a farm in Strand, Iowa. In about 1899, she moved with her parents from Iowa to Landa, ND. She married Tennie Cleven in 1906 and b
2 CONC ecame a farmer's wife. Tennie died of complications of the flu in 1919. In 1923 she married Andrew Surdahl. They continued to live on the farm until he retired in 1946. They moved to Mitchell, SD, for nine months before moving to 
2 CONC Bottineau, ND. Their home in Bottineauwas surrounded by beautiful evergreen trees and flowers. Lizzie was known for her beautiful peonies.
2 CONT
