1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Burial record:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/158589106/betsy-a-schow
2 CONT
2 CONT CLEAR LAKE, Aug 22 – Funeral services for Mrs. Martin P. Schow, 76, were held Friday afternoon at the farm home south of Clear Lake, the Rev. H.O. Urness officiating. Burial was made in the Clear Lake Cemetery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Two selections were presented by Miss Hannah Schonhood, “Jesus Savior Pilot Me” and “Shall We Gather at the River.” Carl Rang and Mrs. Alma Knoblock sang a duet, “Lead Kindly Light.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Schow died Tuesday after an attack. She was born at Decorah March 8, 1855, the daughter of Andrew and Sophia Hetland. Two years after her arrival in Clear Lake in 1876, she was married to Martin Schow. They settled on the far
2 CONC m on which she lived 55 years. Her husband preceded her in death in 1916. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by four sons, John V., Medford, Or.; William C. Garner,; Fred J. and Myron C., Clear Lake, and three daughters, Mrs. Alice Seeger, Mahnomen, Minn.; Mrs. Dora Ladendorf, Chicago, and Mrs. Julia Pya, Stevenson, Briti
2 CONC sh Columbia. One sister, Mrs. Anna Rang, Chicago, is also left. 
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE – Betsey A. Schow was born March 8, 1855 and died August 1831. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcribed by Pat Ludeke
