1 NAME Marion Obed /Ritland/
2 GIVN Marion Obed
2 SURN Ritland
2 _MARNM Ritland
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Fernley
3 STAE Nevada
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 31 JAN 1924
2 ADDR
3 CITY Zearing
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 JUN 2016
2 ADDR
3 CITY Reno
3 STAE Nevada
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Retired
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/167478438/marion-obed-ritland
2 CONT
2 CONT A bright light has gone out in the world with the passing of our beloved Papa Rit. Born in Zearing, Iowa, He grew up in a large and loving family.
2 CONT Rit joined the Army Air Corps in 1942, and shipped out to Europe on the Queen Elizabeth on his 21st birthday. While serving in Europe during WWII, Rit was a P-47 fighter pilot with the 511th fighter squadron of the 405th fighting 
2 CONC group based in Belgium. During the last days of WWII, Rit was shot down over Linz, Austria on his 14th combat mission and taken prisoner by the Germans. When the war was declared over, He was repatriated to his squadron after thre
2 CONC e days as a POW. After the war, Rit flew a P-51 fighter during the occupation of Japan. He retired with the rank of Major from the Air Force in 1966. Rit attended Iowa State and graduated with a Bachelor of Science degree. While s
2 CONC erving in Japan, Rit married Audrey Ilene Ragsdale. The happy couple had two sons, and moved to California, where Rit worked as an aeronautical engineer for McDonnel/Douglas for 30 years, retiring in 1982. Rit spent his retirement
2 CONC  hiking, camping and playing golf. One of the highlights of his later years was a trip he took with his son to Washington D.C. on an Honor Flight for veterans of WWII to visit the war memorials there. Rit is survived by his two so
2 CONC ns and their wives, his brother and sisters. Rit is also survived by his two grandchildren, and his great grandchild. Following Rit's wishes, there will be no services or memorials. His ashes have been interred in the Veterans Cem
2 CONC etary in Fernley, Nevada. If you wish to make any donations in Rits memory, Please make them to the Nevada Honor Flight Foundation at the following website: http:/www.honorflightnv.org/
2 CONT
2 CONT Scroll to the bottom of the page and click on the "donate" button.
2 CONT Published in Reno Gazette-Journal on July 31, 2016
