1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT Lester Cleven
2 CONT
2 CONT May 18, 1915-June 26, 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT BOTTINEAU – Lester Harold Cleven, 92, Burlington, Wash., formerly of Landa, died Tuesday, June 26, 2007, in his home.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born May 18, 1915, to Tennie and Lizzie Cleven in Landa. He married Helen Martinson May 12, 1938, in Minot.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors: wife; daughters, Janice Wysocki, Bottineau; Phyllis Newman, Bellingham, Wash.; Connie Bennington, Steamboat Springs, Colo.; son, Ronald, Burnsville, Minn.; nine grandchildren; seven great-grandchildren; brother, Delno S
2 CONC urdahl, Albuquerque, N.M.; sisters, Olive Jackson, Richland, Wash., Edythe Lonborg, Sequim, Wash.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorial service: July 14 at 1 p.m. in Nero Funeral Home, Bottineau.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial was in Landa Cemetery, Landa.
2 CONT
