2 CONT From Florence Scott''s record:'Ingeborg T. Tjørn did NOT use the surname ''Helgesenupon immigration to the United States, like her oldest brother Hlge Helgesen. On immigration, Ingeborg used T. Tjørn like her brothers Iver T. Tjør
2 CONC n and Thomas T. Tjørn. The T stands for Tønnes, her father, and Tjørn is the farm name. The Helgesen name is derived from Helge, the name of Tønnes' father. HelgeSON is the Americanized spelling of the Norwegian surname Helgesen. 
2 CONC The Ship Manifest states that Ingeborg entered the United States with $10 and that she was scheduled to join her sister, Sophie (Mrs Lars Watne) in Cooperstown, North Dakota, US. Ellis Island (Immigration) Passenger Record: Date o
2 CONC f arrival: Mar 20, 1905 Ship of Travel: Lucania (S7S Lucania, Cunard Line) Port of Departure: Liverpool Manifest Line Number: 0011
