1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Vaccinated 18 July 1888. Confirmed 6 October 1901. Twin of Mandius.
2 CONT
2 CONT Used the surname Helgeson in USA. Jonas immigrated to the USA at age 18, arriving 24 february 1905 on the ship Baltic, which had departed from Liverpool. Ellis Island immigration records reversed names listing him as Tjørn Jonas. 
2 CONC He entered the US with $10 and the final destination listed on the ship manifest was Cooperstown, North Dakota where his sister Sophie (Mrs Lars Vatne) lived. As a US citizen, the World War 1 Draft Registration Crad shows Jonas wa
2 CONC s drafted 5 June 1917. Th draft card describes Jonas as having blue eyes, dark brown hair and of medium height. Jonas returned from a Norway trip, arriving in New York 26 July 1948 aboard the ship Stavangerfjord.
