1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dødsnotis i avis:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.ancestry.com/search/obit/view.aspx?db=web-obituary&kw=&pid=22041246&url=http://search.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/sse.dll%3Fdb%3dweb-obituary%26ti%3d0%26gss%3dangs-i%26ssrc%3dgr_t26158296_p1872466520_ktidz0q3d26158296z0q26pidz
2 CONC 0q3d1872466520z0q26pgz0q3d32799z0q252c32842z0q26pgPLz0q3dtidz0q257cpidz0q26pgPSz0q3d1872466520_h5601786115
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodore Slettebo
2 CONT
2 CONT Tuesday, November 17, 2009 7:07 AM MST
2 CONT
2 CONT Aug. 22, 1927 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nov. 13, 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodore (Ted) Slettebo, born in Big Timber, Mont., Aug. 22, 1927, entered into the service of our Lord Nov. 13.
2 CONT
2 CONT First Sgt. (Army Retired 1945-1977) Slettebo died of natural causes in Lake Havasu City under the care of Hospice of Havasu at the Polidori House.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a great man of honor and a defender for the fight for freedom for the United States of America. He loved his country very much and showed this by flying our flag wherever he was.
2 CONT
2 CONT He proudly served in World War II, the Korean War and Vietnam. He even tried to re-enlist during the first Gulf War. He will be greatly missed by all who knew him and especially by his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his children; John, Cynthia, Deborah Rae, Pamela, Kimberly, Debra Ann and Michael; along with 13 grandchildren and 16 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents, Theodore Slettebo, Louise and Knute Hogamark; and sisters, Evelyn Myrstol and Thelma Mossness; and his soul mate, Sylvia E. Slettebo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dad, you are free now and though we will miss you very much we know we all will be together some day. You were and will remain a true American hero. And we simply called you dad.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be held at the Southern Nevada Veterans Memorial Cemetery in Boulder City, Nev., Wednesday at 8:40 a.m. In lieu of flowers, please make donations to Hospice of Havasu, Polidori House, PO Box 597, Lake Havasu City, AZ
2 CONC  86405.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thoughts and condolences may be submitted to the family at www.lietz-frazefuneralhome.com.
