1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [https://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/ft/person/pf01052238000032 Norway census 1875] - "Ole Grøsfjeld Gabrielsen", born "Sogendals Ladested", Rogaland, Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/4:1:K698-WWV FamilySearch Family Tree] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 10 2017, 8:01:02 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole Gabrielson Grosfield immigrated when he was 17, on 6 May, 1889, he arrived in the U.S. on the steamer Umbria, landing in N. Y. from Liverpool. FAIRVIEW ENTERPRISE (FAIRVIEW, KANSAS) 3 SEPT, 1931, THU PAGE 3
2 CONT
2 CONT THE ATCHISON DAILY GLOBE (ATCHISON, KANSAS) 18 MAY, 1950 THU PAGE 5
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole Grosfield, 78, died Tuesday evening of a heart attack at his farm home north of Everest. He was apparently in his usual health and was doing his evening chores when stricken, about 6:30 p.m. He told his son, Henry, he wasn’t f
2 CONC eeling well and slumped to the ground, death coming at once. Funeral services will be held tomorrow at 1:45 p.m. at the Rake Funeral Home in Horton and at 2:30 p.m. at the Zion Lutheran church, the Rev. J. P. Langsjoen officiating
2 CONC . Burial will be in the Zion cemetery. He was born in Sogndal, Norway, Nov. 14, 1871, and on Feb 27, 1897, married Severina Peterson, whose death occurred March 14, 1942. After her death he made his home with his son, Henry. Survi
2 CONC ving are two brothers, Benjamin Grosfield, Everest, and Gabriel Grosfield, Duchess, Alberta, Canada; two daughters, Mrs. Albert Knudson, Willis, and Mrs. J. G. Jacobson, Horton; two sons, Henry and Oscar, Willis.
