1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From "Find A Grave":
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:  Mar. 11, 1881 Stavanger Stavanger kommune Rogaland fylke, Norway  Death:  Oct. 25, 1938 Big Timber Sweet Grass County Montana, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Guri Ueland Langhus passed at the Langhus home in this city Tuesday evening, after a lingering illness of cancer. Burial will be held from the Lutheran church in this city Saturday at 2:30 p. m. Deceased was born in Stavanger
2 CONC , Norway, March 11, 1881. Twenty five years ago she came to Montana, Sweet Grass county, and had resided here continuously since, their country home being on Big Timber creek near the Crazy mountains.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral service for Mrs. Ole J. Langhus, a most estimable wife and mother, whose death was announced in last week's Pioneer, was held at the Lutheran church in this city Saturday afternoon. Rev. A. A. Holbeck conducted the service
2 CONC , many friends, and neighbors attending. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Musical selections were given by Mrs. Signa. C Bailey and Mrs. Margaret Busha, Mrs. Frank Chase accompanist. Burial was in Mountain View, pallbearers being Nils Hellern and John Stene of Columbus; Anton Solberg, Louis Wesland, Joh
2 CONC n Boe and C. O. Loftsgaarden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to a husband, deceased leaves three daughters and one son. The children are Olga, Guri, inga and Sam all at home. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Ole J Langhus (1876 - 1952)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Inga Langhus Boe (1916 - 2002)*
2 CONT   Guri Langhus (1920 - 2001)*
2 CONT   Olga Langhus (1922 - 2013)* 
